<title>RUSSIA: Russian titanium sponge output soars in 1996.</title>
<headline>Russian titanium sponge output soars in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-03-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Titanium sponge output at Russia's AVISMA plant soared 42 percent in 1996 to 20,000 tonnes, Interfax news agency said on Monday.</p>
<p>It quoted plant board member Alexander Gusev as saying that the enterprise boosted output to match export demand and that it would do so through 1998.</p>
<p>No production forecasts were provided for 1997.</p>
<p>AVISMA is part of the Rosprom financial-industrial group.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
